course: dictionary
lesson: 7865
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word rain can be a noun or a verb. As a noun, rain is the water that falls from clouds in drops. As a verb, it rains: water falls from the sky and the ground gets wet.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is right. «Donkey coats are not waterproof like horses' coats, so donkeys need shelter from the rain.» Here rain is the water falling from the clouds, because donkeys need shelter from wet weather.
explain: Rain can also mean a lot of something falling, like «a rain of arrows». Check your meaning by putting it in the sentence: a lot of arrows falling makes sense. Always test the meaning you choose.
explain: Some rain phrases do not mean weather at all. In the USA, a «rain check» means doing something another time. The words around it tell you that, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Rain is water that falls from clouds in drops.
fact: «Il pleut des cordes» is French for heavy rain; it means "it's raining ropes".
fact: Each year, wildebeest follow the rain and fresh grass round the Serengeti and the Masai Mara.
fact: Donkeys need shelter from the rain because their coats are not waterproof like horses' coats.
fact: Ireland's frequent rain keeps its grass green all year.
exercise: «Donkey coats are not waterproof like horses' coats, so donkeys need shelter from the rain.» What is rain in this sentence? | *Water that falls from clouds in drops | A rain check for later | A rain of arrows | To stop doing something
exercise: «Its frequent rain keeps the grass green all year.» Copy the word that means water falling from clouds. | grass | year | *rain | green
exercise: «In dried-up pools a lungfish sleeps in a ball of mud until the rain comes back.» What does the rain coming back mean? | The pool dries up completely | Mud is washed away by hands | The fish wakes up and swims away | *Water starts falling from the clouds again
test: «Heavy rain is il pleut des cordes.» What does this French phrase mean in English? | A light breeze | Ropes falling from the sky | A dry, sunny day | *Heavy rain
test: Yesterday it ___ all day, so the football match was cancelled. Which word fits? | *rained | rains | rain | raining
exam: In the USA, what does «rain check» mean? | Going out in the rain without a coat | Checking the weather on the radio | *Doing something another time | Water in a bucket left outside
